From: Ben Klopfenstein <benklop@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] configure: detect 32-bit ARM when host_cpu is a bare "arm"

Cross toolchains such as Yocto's arm-poky-linux-gnueabi report host_cpu
as "arm" for 32-bit targets. The "arm" case assumed macOS arm64 and
selected the ARMv8 (AArch64) dynrec backend, which cannot work on a
32-bit target. Ask the compiler whether it targets AArch64, ARMv7+ or
an older ARM and pick the matching backend.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -835,10 +835,29 @@
     c_unalignedmemory=yes
     ;;
    arm) # Mac OS X uname -m says "arm64", for some reason it becomes "arm" ?
+    # Cross toolchains (e.g. Yocto's arm-poky-linux-gnueabi) also report a
+    # bare "arm" for 32-bit targets, so ask the compiler which one it is.
+    AC_COMPILE_IFELSE([AC_LANG_PROGRAM([[
+#ifndef __aarch64__
+#error not aarch64
+#endif
+]])], [
     AC_DEFINE(C_TARGETCPU,ARMV8LE)
     AC_MSG_RESULT(ARMv8 Little Endian 64-bit)
-    c_targetcpu="arm"
     c_unalignedmemory=yes
+    ], [AC_COMPILE_IFELSE([AC_LANG_PROGRAM([[
+#if !defined(__ARM_ARCH) || __ARM_ARCH < 7
+#error pre-ARMv7
+#endif
+]])], [
+    AC_DEFINE(C_TARGETCPU,ARMV7LE)
+    AC_MSG_RESULT(ARMv7 Little Endian)
+    c_unalignedmemory=yes
+    ], [
+    AC_DEFINE(C_TARGETCPU,ARMV4LE)
+    AC_MSG_RESULT(ARMv4 Little Endian)
+    ])])
+    c_targetcpu="arm"
     ;;
    *)
     AC_DEFINE(C_TARGETCPU,UNKNOWN)
